      "message": "you wrapped a loop around a test, but didn\u0027t update any of the existing test failures to say which loop iteration failed. \n\nSee https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/CodeReviewComments#useful-test-failures\n\nI personally would use subtests here, rather than prefacing all test failures with context. They were new in Go 1.7, though, (https://golang.org/doc/go1.7#testing) so you\u0027d need to disable tests here for Go 1.6 and below. I think that\u0027s acceptable. Normally we\u0027d stop our builders testing Go 1.6 when Go 1.8 is releases (Feb 1st), but that\u0027s not too far away.\n\nAlternative, if you prefer, you can write a lowercase testFoo(t *testing.T, ...) func and call it from three capital TestFoo_a, TestFoo_b, TestFoo_c funcs. But that is basically all subtests automate for you.",
